//         in both (A 0.0442, B 0.0450); T6 trough A 3.65, AUC24,ss 119.0, Cmax,ss B 8.95, all PASS against the label (WITH ciclosporin);
//         T7 B:P 11.38 in both, no B:P verdict changed; T9 B not adopted; T10 u(AUC)/AUC 0.1307, u(Cmax)/Cmax 0.40, u(k) 1.83 /h.
//   MISSED: T1 verdict against Djebli 5.25 /h: predicted PASS (fold 1.5) in both, A PASS (ratio 1.21), B FAIL (1.86); T1 k A 6.35 (predicted 4.5, 3.5-6.0), B 9.75 (predicted 5, 4-7), MTT 0.63 and 0.41 h (predicted 0.9);
//         T2 ps scalar A 0.256 (predicted 0.15, 0.10-0.25, just above); T3 Cmax 10 mg A 26.3 (predicted 32, 29-37) and "A closer to 67
//         than B" is false (B 26.7 is higher by 1.3 %); Cmax 6 mg A 16.4 (predicted 19.5, 17-22); C(24 h) 6 mg A 2.91 (predicted 3.45):
//         z -2.74 FAIL, NOT the predicted PASS; T4 t1/2 A 58.2 h (predicted 65, 62-68); T5 Cmax/AUC_inf A 0.0442 (predicted 0.054);
//         T6 Cmax,ss A 9.08 (predicted 10.0, 9.2-11); T8 "C(24 h) FAIL -> PASS" did not happen; T9 the REASON was wrong: rule (i)
//         HOLDS (B has the higher Cmax in both rows, by 1.3 %); it is rule (iii) that fails (4 PASS -> FAIL against 1 FAIL -> PASS).
//   The transit input did NOT raise Cmax in the record refitted to R24: Cmax 10 mg 26.3 (first order 26.1). The first-order
//   Cmax was not limited by the input shape; the R24 fit then absorbs the sharper input by a larger ps scalar.
//   Verdicts in A, old (first-order record) -> new: t1/2 Bottiger PASS -> FAIL (64.7 -> 58.2 h, ratio 0.738 against fold 1.3);
